  "body": "**Status: research note with exact finite computations and a written proof (not a SAT/DRAT proof). No \u03ba claim, no supplier word.** Only `research/a2-family-b-locus/` is added; nothing existing is changed.\n\n## Results\n\n#2784 left open its Claim M (`m \u2265 10`, decoders `M = P Q\u1d40` with factors in the realisation's two 9-dimensional spaces, dense `B`, iff pattern, characteristic 0) on the B-locus `\u03b3\u2082 = \u03b3\u2083` of the A2 family. This closes it.\n\n* **PROVEN (\u00a71):** B-locus members are of B-form, `M = D\u2081G + 1_X \u03b2\u1d40`, `supp \u03b2 \u2286 X`: a rank-one change of the 3\u00d73 triangle block only.\n* **PROVEN from CHECKED facts (a)\u2013(e) (\u00a72):** on the B-locus every such decoder with `m \u2265 10` costs **\u2265 64 (P112), \u2265 72 (E8)**; for P104 (all 28 triangle representatives) **\u2265 58 when the decoder still has \u2265 10 terms after merging parallel terms**, otherwise Theorem F's 56 (so the combined P104 bound stays 56). The key checked input is `Q_XX` = 62 / 56 / 70, the square lower bound with the triangle deleted on both sides (opt3u duality branch-and-bound, complete); the rest is a per-term bound c\u2032 \u2265 7, a class-level inside relaxation (66 / 63 / 75 at 9 terms) and a rank fact on the three triangle normals. The transposed family follows by symmetry.\n* **With #2784 (off the locus 68 / 64 / 77; Theorem F at `m = 9`): Claim M holds on the whole A2 family**: P112 \u2265 64, #968 P104 \u2265 56, E8 \u2265 72, every `m \u2265 9`, factors in the spaces.\n* The relaxation values 62 / 70 (P112 / E8) that made the locus look open are not decoders: the optimum needs three cost-7 terms with row normals \u221d r\u2081, r\u2082, r\u2083 inside an 8-term inside decoder, impossible since they span 2 dimensions. For P104 the value 58 equals the relaxation value.\n\n## Scope and caveats\n\n* Floors for decoders whose realisation `N` is a member of the A2 family and whose factors lie in that realisation's spaces; nothing is claimed for other rank-9 realisations, non-iff patterns or `B` of rank \u2265 10.\n* **Out-of-space `m \u2265 10`** (#2784 \u00a77.3) stays **open**.\n* **Tightness of 64 / 72 on the B-locus is not claimed and was not checked** (the tie decoders of #2784 are off the locus).\n* No \u03ba claim.\n\n## Verification\n\n`bash research/a2-family-b-locus/verify.sh /fresh/dir` (Python \u2265 3.11, `numpy`, `networkx`). On a fresh `git archive` export: **50 PASS, 0 FAIL**, 172 s wall (`nice 10`; the 28 P104 representatives and the `Q_XX` partial punctures run 6 at a time, each under `timeout 1200`). It re-runs facts (a)\u2013(e) including `Q_XX` on P112, E8 and all 28 P104 representatives (outputs compared byte-for-byte with the recorded logs), the relaxation with the `e\u2089` row and column, and the inside relaxation. The needed files of #2784 (`a2lib`, `opt3u` and their imports) are vendored unchanged so the package is self-contained (`NOTICE.md`, `SOURCES.json`, `MANIFEST.sha256`).\n\n## Overlap\n\nFollow-up to #2784 (ours); parents #2338, #2724, #2277 (ours). Cited: #968. No other overlap expected.\n\nPrepared by DreamingOfClouds with Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic), via Claude Code; Apache-2.0.\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
